jablow@pilot.njin.net (Eric Jablow), <Jul.3.22.25.05.1990.6900@pilot.njin.net>:
:I've noticed a couple of wierd things about PC Nethack PL8.
:
:1.	The PrintScreen key doesn't seem to work.  I want to printout
:the level map, and nothing happens.  Is it my machine, or a game bug?
     Nethack traps PrintScreens (^P) in order to give you the previous
message. You can defeat this (sometimes accidentally; it freezes your
game if you don't have a printer) by typing, say, 'i^p' in rapid
succession.  With any luck, you'll manage the ^p while the game is
consulting its overlay as far as how to display an inventory, and you'll
get an intact map.

:2.	When I found a shop with "Closed for Inventory" engraved
:outside the door, I left the area.  Still, the cash register
:occasionally chimed.  Isn't that a little strange?  
     Think of it as the shopkeeper testing his cash register or checking
his cash supply.

:About the people who want to have some "automatic commands", why don't
:we add to the wish list for the next version a macro processor.  Let's
:allow commands to be bound to the function keys, where available.  In
:fact, let skilled players execute macros faster--practice making
:perfect.
     I'm all for changing the interface this way (macros should probably
abort when a player is hit by anything-- perhaps an option), but not the
actual game balance.

